internal/**/*.json text eol=lf
internal/**/*.tmpl text eol=lf

# Issue #1294. `git grep` skips a file it thinks is binary, printing
# "Binary file X matches" - a match with no line, which a sweep piping to
# `wc -l` counts as one instead of N. Plain grep skips it in total silence.
# live/e2e/corpus-mastino-dns/run.sh carried four NUL bytes in 159,562 and
# cost three sweeps (#1157, #1214, #1291) before anyone noticed. The bytes
# are gone and live/grepblind_test.go now fails any swept shell script that
# acquires one, but this makes `git grep` read a shell script in full even
# in the window before that guard runs.
*.sh text eol=lf diff

# Issue #1308. Four files here are written only by `go run ./tools/gauntlet
# render` from live/gauntlet.json. Two branches that each moved a verdict
# produce two different renders of the same derived bytes, and git's
# line-based merge either conflicts - six resolutions on 2026-09-18 across
# five branches, all resolved identically - or, worse, succeeds hunk by
# hunk and hands back a board assembled from both sides that no render ever
# produced. The driver keeps our side whole instead; the re-render that
# follows is what settles the content, and TestRenderedDocsAreCurrent fails
# until it happens.
#
# Merge drivers are per-clone configuration: `just merge-drivers` installs
# this one, and without it git falls back to the ordinary line merge. It
# does nothing for a merge GitHub performs on its own servers. The guard
# that holds everywhere is in the test suite, not here.
live/GAUNTLET.md merge=gauntlet-rendered
site/data/gauntlet.json merge=gauntlet-rendered
site/data/gauntlet_board.json merge=gauntlet-rendered
site/data/gauntlet_scale.json merge=gauntlet-rendered
